Implement reusable exact polynomial differential operators in src/differential.rs.
Manual PDD prompt-first implementation, no provider/regeneration claim. Only own src/differential.rs, tests/differential_operators.rs, prompts/differential_rust.prompt, docs/DIFFERENTIAL.md; parent owns exports/config.
Use existing BigPoly/BigC/BigQ and shared Budget/Error; no dependencies, floats, legacy panic ops.
Expose differentiate(&BigPoly,&str,&mut Budget)->Result<BigPoly>. DifferentialOperator<const N:usize> has private coords:[String;N], terms:BTreeMap<[u16;N],BigPoly>. Fallible constructors from_terms(coords,owned map,b), partial(coords,axis:usize,b), multiplication(coords,owned BigPoly,b). Methods try_add/try_sub/compose/commutator(&self,&Self,b), try_scale(&self,&BigPoly,b), apply(&self,&BigPoly,b), terms()->&BTreeMap, coords()->&[String;N]. All algebra uses final mutable Budget, returns Result<Self> except apply returns Result<BigPoly>.
Right-normalized derivatives are ordinary coordinate partials. Composition self after rhs uses full multivariate Leibniz sum binomial(alpha,gamma)*a_alpha*(D^gamma b_beta)*D^(alpha-gamma+beta). Normalize/delete zeros; commutator AB-BA. Symbols outside coordinates are constant parameters.
Reject dimension0/>16, empty/duplicate names, invalid axes, context mismatches before algebra. Hard total derivative order32, also shared Degree/WordLength. Terms bounds aggregate operator entries plus coefficient monomials; InputBytes bounds coordinate bytes plus coefficient symbol occurrences. Validate operands even if output zero. Charge deterministic validation/enumeration/cloning and exact coefficient arithmetic before growth. Flat representation has no recursive expression depth; WordLength limits derivative depth. Exact rationals cannot represent NaN/infinity. No unbounded recursion or unchecked binomial growth.
Specialized <4>::orbital_lorentz(coords,mu,nu,hbar:BigQ,b)=-i*hbar*(x^mu partial^nu-x^nu partial^mu); momentum(coords,mu,hbar,b)=-i*hbar*partial^mu; eta diagonal(-1,1,1,1), stored derivative indices use lower partials.
Tests cover exact/product/mixed derivatives, multivariate binomial coefficients, second-derivative commutator cancellation, every Lorentz/Poincare component, arbitrary polynomial witnesses, invalid/budget cases. Document identities for formal commuting partials/arbitrary smooth fields, not general quantum domain or central-charge proof.
